      "text": "Roe began as a railroad depot around 1880 on the Cotton Belt, becoming the first depot south of Clarendon in Monroe County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roe%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally in Prairie County, a 1883 boundary change moved Roe into Monroe County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roe%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Roe sits on the northern edge of the Grand Prairie, a flat, fertile plain that was among Arkansas’s last settled areas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/roe_arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town experiences a humid subtropical climate, with hot, humid summers and mild to cool winters.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
